# VAR-DATA-001 deterministic varied-action schedule closed-editor evidence

Date: 2026-09-02
Engine/project: Unreal Engine 5.8.2 / Game Animation Sample

## Build

- Deployed repository `unreal/Plugins/MotionWorld` into the closed sample project.
- Built `GameAnimationSampleEditor Mac Development -architecture=arm64+x86_64`.
- Result: Succeeded; 60/60 actions; universal MotionWorld dylib produced.

## Automation

- Command filter: `Automation RunTests MotionWorld.`
- Tests discovered: 12.
- Final result: 12 Success, 0 Fail.
- New test: `MotionWorld.Collection.VariedActionSchedule` — Success.
- Raw Unreal log: `motionworld_varied_schedule_automation_fixed.log` under the local Unreal log tree.

## Reviewer finding preserved

The first headless run had 11 successes and one failure in the new schedule test. Repeatedly adding
0.8 and 0.4 seconds made the accumulated 4.8-second boundary differ from the independently written
4.8 timestamp by one floating-point representation step. This could also disagree with the
closed-form automatic-completion duration. The implementation now computes every phase boundary
from explicit closed-form sums shared with the duration semantics. The rebuilt rerun passed all 12.

## Scope

This proves compilation, pure schedule semantics, fail-closed configuration, and regression safety.
It does not prove live character behavior, episode export, action coverage, or schema-loader
acceptance. Those remain the live episode 4101 gate.
